{"nodes": [{"id": "security_document", "label": "SECURITY.md (Response Header Rationale)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "security_content_security_policy", "label": "Content-Security-Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defends against token theft via localStorage-based auth tokens and the app's contentEditable/innerHTML rendering of user-authored HTML; acts as a second line of defense behind the sanitiser. Fails closed: a mistake breaks the app rather than degrading security."}, {"id": "security_script_src", "label": "script-src 'self'", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Load-bearing CSP line. No 'unsafe-inline' or 'unsafe-eval', which is why the theme guard was moved from an inline script block to public/theme-init.js as a separate file. A bypass of the sanitiser then only injects inert markup instead of executing script."}, {"id": "security_style_src", "label": "style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The one real compromise in the policy: allows inline styles because Framer Motion animates via style attributes and the app sets colors from data. Exposure is smaller than script-src's because injected CSS can restyle but not read tokens."}, {"id": "security_connect_src", "label": "connect-src 'self' https: wss:", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately broad because the API origin is a build-time variable (VITE_API_URL); pinning it here would create lockstep-edit failure risk where every request gets blocked. https:/wss: still forbid plaintext exfiltration."}, {"id": "security_img_media_src", "label": "img-src / media-src allow https:", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "User uploads are served from Cloudflare R2 on a bucket-specific hostname configured outside this file; blob:/data: are needed by the client-side image downscaler before an upload is presigned."}, {"id": "security_lockdown_directives", "label": "object-src 'none', base-uri 'self', frame-ancestors 'none', form-action 'self'", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The four directives that cost nothing: close plugin embedding, base-tag hijacking, clickjacking, and third-party form posts."}, {"id": "security_upgrade_insecure_requests", "label": "upgrade-insecure-requests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Belt and braces alongside HSTS."}, {"id": "security_token_storage_localstorage", "label": "Access/refresh tokens stored in localStorage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepted trade-off: the API and PWA are on different origins, so httpOnly; SameSite=None cookies are third-party and blocked by Safari/Chrome. Consequence: any script executing on this origin can read both tokens."}, {"id": "security_contenteditable_innerhtml_pattern", "label": "contentEditable + innerHTML rendering of user HTML", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Described as the highest-risk pattern in the codebase; user-authored HTML is rendered into a contentEditable and mounted with innerHTML."}, {"id": "security_sanitiser", "label": "Sanitiser (client + server)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A real sanitiser exists on both sides of the wire and is considered good, but is a single point of failure; CSP is the second point of failure behind it."}, {"id": "security_hsts", "label": "Strict-Transport-Security", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Set for a year including subdomains; standard, and required for the HSTS preload list if ever wanted."}, {"id": "security_x_content_type_options", "label": "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stops a browser from deciding an uploaded file is HTML because it looks like it."}, {"id": "security_x_frame_options", "label": "X-Frame-Options: DENY", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Redundant with frame-ancestors for modern browsers; kept for older ones."}, {"id": "security_referrer_policy", "label": "Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Project ids live in URLs; this keeps them out of third-party Referer headers."}, {"id": "security_permissions_policy", "label": "Permissions-Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Camera, microphone, geolocation and FLoC all off; the app asks for none of them."}, {"id": "security_cache_control_assets", "label": "Cache-Control on /assets/*", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Content-hashed filenames make a year plus immutable safe."}, {"id": "security_cache_control_sw", "label": "Cache-Control on /sw.js", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The opposite of asset caching: the service worker must always be revalidated, or a bad one pins itself."}, {"id": "security_httponly_cookie_fix", "label": "Structural fix: httpOnly cookie on shared parent domain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The refresh token is still reachable by script on this origin. The real fix is moving it to an httpOnly cookie on a shared parent domain, requiring the API to be hosted at api.<same-domain> as the PWA. Until then, the CSP is mitigation, not cure."}, {"id": "vercel_json", "label": "vercel.json", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "public_theme_init_js", "label": "public/theme-init.js", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "shared_api_token_store", "label": "shared/api/token-store.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "security_script_src", "target": "security_content_security_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_style_src", "target": "security_content_security_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_connect_src", "target": "security_content_security_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_img_media_src", "target": "security_content_security_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_lockdown_directives", "target": "security_content_security_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_upgrade_insecure_requests", "target": "security_content_security_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_upgrade_insecure_requests", "target": "security_hsts", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_x_frame_options", "tar